  "text": "Member-only story\nChatGPT Is Poisoning Your Brain...\nHere’s How to Stop It Before It’s Too Late.\n5 min read · Apr 30, 2025\nJordan Gibbs\nFollow\nGenerated by the author with AI.\nChatGPT’s tendency to be overly supportive and encouraging is eating your…\n[Uncaptured paragraphs omitted]\nA ChatGPT session is an echo chamber to end all other echo chambers — it’s just you, an overly friendly AI, and all your thoughts, dreams, desires, and secrets endlessly affirmed, validated, and supported.\nWhy is this dangerous? Well, like any feedback loop, it becomes vicious. One day you’re casually brainstorming some ideas with ChatGPT, and the next you’re sucked into a delusion of grandeur.\nA real screenshot from a recent GPT session...\n[Uncaptured paragraphs omitted]\nMaybe I’m being a little dramatic here. However, even on a small scale, this feedback loop can be problematic, especially if you’re like me and use LLMs daily.\nI’m writing this article to help you be as conscious of this problem as possible, and to give you some prompts to avoid it.\n· · ·\nThis “yes man” problem has existed since the birth of ChatGPT, but it was brought to the public eye at large last week when a simple platform-wide system prompt update from OpenAI made it so much worse.\nChatGPT is inherently programmed to be a yes man… it’s a sycophant, your biggest fan, and most undying supporter for a reason.\n[Uncaptured paragraphs omitted]\nI hope these prompts can help you escape the ChatGPT confirmation bias trap, and focus on true growth.\nThanks for reading!\n-Jordan\nChatGPT\nAI\nArtificial Intelligence\nOpenAI\nProductivity\nFollow\nWritten by Jordan Gibbs\n10.2K followers · 24 following\nNeed an AI prototype ASAP? Let's chat.\nhttps://jordangibbs.xyz\nResponses (7)\n예시 독자 A\nWhat are your thoughts?\nBérnie\nApr 29, 2025\nYes, Claude is like this too. Open AI already said today (on X) that they've tweaked the AI a little and it should be improving this week. The AI should be more like a professor/counsellor/business partner working with you not as a friend who will agree with everything you do.\n1K\n1 replies\nReply\nSunil Bajpai\nApr 30, 2025\nSpot on! Consultants do the same because they need to get hired by you :-)\n844\nReply\nAlfred Akech\nMay 2, 2025 (edited)\nGreat read! I could not agree more. I just wrote about this, but you beat me to it 👏.\nThe way AI functions today must change. Who knows…\nRead more...\n733\n1 replies\nReply\nSee all responses\nMore from Jordan Gibbs\nJordan Gibbs\nBehold...The Prompt Bible is Here\nThe Most Useful Tips from Google’s Epic 70-Page AI Prompt Engineering Guide\nMay 24\n670\n0\nJordan Gibbs\nChatGPT Users...Should You Make the Switch to Gemini?\nReading tools · local example\n18K\n7\nMedium · Mock\nMedium Rules\nM\nMedium Policy\nMedium Rules\n11 min read · May 26, 2021\nM\nMedium\nFollow\nMedium is an open platform that exists to share ideas and perspectives from the world’s most insightful writers, thinkers, and storytellers.\nWe welcome thoughtful and civil discussion from a broad spectrum of viewpoints. To maintain a safe, respectful, and welcoming environment for a wide range of people to engage in meaningful conversations, we prohibit certain conduct.\nIn deciding whether there has been a violation of the rules, we will take into consideration things like newsworthiness,\nThis is an excerpt. The current rules may have changed.\nLocal preview · interactions are mock. The captured 272 responses are not included.\nRead the current Medium Rules\n54K\n0"
